            "notes": "*Your point was holdin',\nRipped jeans, Mercy showin'*\n\nBecause sometimes you might end up payload princess, and cash changes, round 3 can be a bit hard to predict how much money you'll have.\n\nGo with Vishkar if you at all can, as well as Multi-tool for the cooldown. Nano Cola is great if you can afford it. If you're rich, you can do Divine Intervention with Vishkar if you're dying a lot. Possibly unpopular opinion but if you're REALLY dying, you can just do Vishkar and Divine even if you're not rich, and just fill up however much AP you can scrounge with blues and greens. You are no good to your team if you're going 0-5.\n\nIf you're against a good Tracer or Genji, it's okay to just swap from shields to armor for the damage reduction. You can also take the reduced critical hits from Iron if you have Tracer and/or Soldier with autoaim shredding you. As I said in the build notes, a lot of how this works is understanding WHY you are choosing things instead of just mindlessly following a build someone else made.\n\n**The only caveat with that is if they catch on and take Codebreaker to ignore your armor, switch back to shields to deny them.**",
